  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\pi -(-\\pi )=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n2\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,\u27f9\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{2\\pi }=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $1$ unit up. Hence, $D=1.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(\\frac{x}{2})+1.\n$$",
